## 🧠✨ Reflective Learning Journey

This repository reflects my practical SQL learning journey alongside my MSc in Health Informatics and clinical background.

The project progresses from fundamental SQL concepts to more advanced analytical techniques. The later sections introduce concepts that are still relatively new to me, including:

- Common Table Expressions (CTEs)
- Window Functions
- Executive reporting
- Advanced analytical queries
- Advanced CASE logic
- Risk scoring methodologies
- Executive reporting
- Analytical SQL design

To strengthen my understanding, I actively supplement my learning through structured SQL study, technical documentation and hands-on practice using platforms such as GeeksforGeeks alongside MySQL Workbench.

Rather than simply completing tutorials, my goal is to apply newly learned concepts within realistic healthcare, CRM and governance scenarios. I believe documenting this progression is an honest reflection of both my current ability and my commitment to continuous professional development.
